        "department": "CSE",
        "description": "The aim of this course is to study state-of-the-art software stacks and compilers developed to host machine/deep learning workloads. Students will learn the architecture of the Tensorflow framework for deep learning workloads. We will also discuss an ML compiler, Apache TVM, and intermediate representations specifically designed for ML applications, such as MLIR, Relay, and TensorIR. In addition, tensor accelerators, such as TPUs and GPUs, will also be discussed. The class lectures will be based on research papers, and evaluation will be done using class participation. This course is suitable for students interested in systems research and paper reading.",
